  "_comment": [
    "Quiz options the engine returned unchanged: the English string is still",
    "standing where French carries a translated one ('Le Cri' -> 'The Scream').",
    "Keyed by language, then by the option exactly as the pack spells it today.",
    "Each rendering follows the wording the question's own explanation already",
    "uses, so the option and the sentence that justifies it agree.",
    "Names that stay in the original everywhere - the ship Ever Given, the group",
    "Furious Five, the Nation of Islam, the Old Vic, the Soft Power 30 index -",
    "keep their name and only lose the English article the target language does",
    "not write.",
    "\"_shared\" applies to every language that does not list the option itself: French names that arrived with their accents stripped, which no Latin-script locale spells that way. Napoléon and Hô Chi Minh are deliberately not here - outside French those are written Napoleon and Ho Chi Minh.",
    "The languages that write no Latin at all keep a longer tail: a single Latin word needs no article to give it away, so Hubris, Bebop and Odoacer are left standing there where an article would have been translated away."
  ],
